In article <4630.27539276@cc.nu.oz.au> c8730752@cc.nu.oz.au writes:
>someone please tell me how to use the wizard mode
>(PC v3pl9)
>tried and didn't work:
>1. typed "nethack", gave name as "wizard" and chose wizard character
>2. typed "nethack -D" and ditto   (discovery mode)

Ok.  The key here is to do BOTH things at the same time.  Like so:

	nethack -u Wizard -D <cr>

Note carefully the capitalization of Wizard and of "-D".  By the way, -u is
the nethack flag to "use" the following name.  This means that you're stuck
with the name "Wizard", but your score will not go onto the record file
anyway, so ...

Enjoy!
